<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrea Gritti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1455">1455</a>–<a href="/years/1538">1538</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrea Gritti was Doge of the Venetian Republic from 1523 to 1538. A grain merchant in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> for almost twenty years, he represented <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> at the Ottoman court and in 1499 was imprisoned for sending coded reports on the Ottoman navy, escaping execution through his friendship with the grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a>. As provveditore generale in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cambrai">War of the League of Cambrai</a> he recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> in July 1509, a feat that opened his way to the dogeship. As doge he made a treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> that ended Venice's active part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a>, but could not keep the Republic out of a new Ottoman war after Suleiman I attacked Corfu in 1537.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andrea-gritti.jpg" alt="Andrea Gritti" width="330" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Titian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ritratto_del_Doge_Andrea_Gritti_-_Tiziano_059.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
